# `tot fmt` writes LF — see "Canonical form" in SPEC.md. On a CRLF checkout the formatter
# would rewrite every file on sight and `tot fmt --check` could never pass, because git would
# convert the LF output straight back to CRLF. Checking out with LF is what keeps the
# formatter and the working tree agreeing, on Windows as well as anywhere else.
*.tot text eol=lf
*.rs text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
